<title>INDIA: India 97/98 fiscal deficit target 4.5 pct/GDP.</title>
<headline>India 97/98 fiscal deficit target 4.5 pct/GDP.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian Finance Minister P. Chidambaram said on Friday that the government has set a fiscal deficit target of 4.5 percent of gross domestic product (GDP) for 1997/98 (April-March).  </p>
<p>Chidambaram told parliament that the government aims to cut the fiscal deficit as a share of GDP to below 4.0 percent in 1998/99.</p>
<p>Earlier, the finance minister said the estimate of the 1996/97 fiscal deficit as a proportion of GDP remained unchanged at 5.0 percent.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
